+//! WOW-BG3 (local fork, patch 0005): BG3's own effects replayed inside WoW.
+//! Spell effects must look exactly as in BG3, drawn into WoW's world, "1:1 like
+//! SkyCraft". The BG3 capture layer (`bg3/capture`, format in `link/benilla/fx-replay-format.md`)
+//! records every effect draw near Tav: `fxframe.bin` each BG3 frame in `$WOW_BG3_TAV_DIR`
+//! (default `/tmp/wowbg3/tav`), and once per key the pipeline recipes, SPIR-V modules, samplers
+//! and textures under `$WOW_BG3_FX_DIR` (default the capture directory's `fx/`).
+//!
+//! This half runs in the main world: it reads and decodes the newest frame, loads and caches
+//! what the frame names (recipes, SPIR-V with its reflection and a Y-flipped vertex variant,
+//! samplers, textures), and hands the lot to the render world as [`FxExtract`]. The render
+//! world (`wowbg3_fx_render`) replays the draws with BG3's own shaders through wgpu's SPIR-V
+//! passthrough and composites them over the world camera's view.
+//!
+//! Y: BG3 draws with a positive Vulkan viewport (clip +Y down) while wgpu flips every viewport
+//! (clip +Y up), so each vertex module is patched to negate `Position.y` before it is stored
+//! ([`flip_position_y`]). Framebuffer positions, winding and `FragCoord` then match BG3's
+//! exactly and BG3's cull mode and front face pass through unchanged.
+//!
+//! TAA: BG3 jitters its projection every frame; [`strip_jitter`] takes that out of the per-view
+//! constants so the replayed effects hold still. Colours: the frame's post block ("FXQ1") gives
+//! BG3's exposure, grading and display LUTs, which the composite uses (`wowbg3_fx_render`).
+//!
+//! Camera: the world camera follows BG3's camera record (`bg3cam.bin`, `wowbg3_lead`), and each
+//! frame's post block names the record BG3 drew it with (`bg3cam_seq`). The last few frames are
+//! kept and the one drawn with the record the camera follows this frame is replayed
+//! ([`pick_frame`]), so the effects stay put on WoW's world while the camera moves.
+//!
+//! A frame older than half a second (BG3 stopped or restarting) draws nothing, and so does every
+//! frame while the world camera does not follow BG3's.
+
+use std::collections::{HashMap, HashSet, VecDeque};
+use std::path::PathBuf;
+use std::sync::Arc;
+use std::time::{Duration, Instant, SystemTime, UNIX_EPOCH};
+
+use benilla_world::view::WorldCamera;
+use bevy::prelude::*;
+use bevy::render::extract_component::{ExtractComponent, ExtractComponentPlugin};
+use bevy::render::extract_resource::{ExtractResource, ExtractResourcePlugin};
+use bevy::render::render_resource::TextureUsages;
+
+/// A frame whose BG3 wall time is older than this draws nothing.
+const STALE_SECS: f64 = 0.5;
+/// How long a missing recipe, module, sampler or texture waits before it is looked for again.
+const RETRY: Duration = Duration::from_secs(2);
+/// Texture bytes read per frame at most (the rest waits for the next frames).
+const TEX_BUDGET: usize = 48 << 20;
+/// Files larger than this are refused.
+const MAX_FILE: u64 = 512 << 20;
+/// Texture keys up to this are BG3's per-frame targets, not files (format doc, "Special keys").
+const SPECIAL_KEYS: u64 = 5;
+/// Decoded frames kept to pair with the camera record ([`pick_frame`]).
+const HISTORY: usize = 8;
